{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_deriv_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_deriv_symm","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRogersReflection.lean#L85-L95","doc":"The derivative is invariant under `x ↦ 1 - x` up to sign — the symmetry that\nmakes `rogersL_reflection` true, stated so it is visible rather than implicit.\n\nIt needs no hypotheses at all: the first draft carried `0 < x < 1` by reflex and\nthe linter caught them unused. The symmetry is algebraic; only the *derivative\nformula* it is applied to needs the interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.hasDerivAt_rogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.hasDerivAt_rogersL","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRogersReflection.lean#L67-L83","doc":"**The Rogers derivative**, `L'(x) = -(log(1-x)/x + log x/(1-x))/2` on `(0,1)`.\n\nThe half in the Rogers normalisation is what makes this symmetric under\n`x ↦ 1 - x`, which is the analytic content of `rogersL_reflection` above and the\nstarting point for any proof of the five-term relation — the one input the\nlevel-7 numerators still lack (`qou-rhyp`, `FiveTwoFiveTermArguments.lean`).\n\nBoth ingredients are already sorry-free in `QOU/Archimedean/DilogReflection.lean`;\nthis is a product rule and a `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRogersReflection.lean#L61-L65","doc":"The form the ladder file consumes: `L (1 − x) = L1 − L x` with `L1 = π²/6`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_reflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL_reflection","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRogersReflection.lean#L49-L59","doc":"**Rogers reflection**, from `LiTwo_reflection'`.\n\nThe Euler correction term `−log x · log(1−x)` is cancelled exactly by the two\nhalf-`log·log` terms in the Rogers normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRogersReflection.rogersL","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRogersReflection.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The Rogers dilogarithm, built from the corpus's real `LiTwo`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}